     1	#!/usr/bin/env python3
     2	"""Mechanical FINALS RULE check (dec 087 item 1, clause (b)), v2 (strict; codex review 091327).
     3	
     4	A candidate final qualifies via a COMPLETE-scored reference bundle only if the two zips are
     5	byte-identical except for single-line value changes of these knobs, each <= the reference value:
     6	  eval_config.yaml (zip root)   evaluation.max_time_minutes / max_tool_calls / max_turns
     7	  agent config documents         generate_content_config.max_output_tokens /
     8	  (agent.yaml + every sub-agent  generate_content_config.thinking_config.thinking_budget
     9	   reached via agent_tool         (inline, or in the file named by a top-level
    10	   config_path, recursively)      `generate_content_config: !include F`: max_output_tokens /
    11	                                  thinking_config.thinking_budget at that file's top level)
    12	Rules (all conservative -> INELIGIBLE):
    13	- Zip entries: unique names (also case-folded), normalized relative POSIX paths, regular files only
    14	  (no directory entries, symlinks or other types, no encryption), no file/directory conflicts.
    15	  The candidate and reference must have the same entry names.
    16	- Every file not listed above must be byte-identical. A listed file may differ only on lines of the
    17	  form `<indent><knob>: <number><trailing>` with identical prefix/suffix bytes, same line count; the
    18	  changed value node must sit exactly at an allowed path (checked on the composed YAML node tree;
    19	  duplicate mapping keys rejected). Comments, quoting, anchors, aliases, flow style: must be identical.
    20	- Domains: max_output_tokens, max_tool_calls, max_turns int >= 1; thinking_budget int >= 0;
    21	  max_time_minutes number > 0. No leading zeros, no sign, no exponent/underscore.
    22	- Include / config_path targets are resolved both root-relative and relative to the containing
    23	  document; if both resolutions exist as different entries the target is ambiguous and gets no
    24	  allowance (must stay byte-identical).
    25	
    26	Clause (a) (the candidate itself scored COMPLETE) is not checked here; --reference-lb checks that
    27	the reference has status COMPLETE and that its sha256 matches the reference zip.
    28	
    29	Usage: eval/finals_eligibility.py CANDIDATE.zip REFERENCE.zip [--reference-lb results/lb_X.json]
    30	                                  [--out results/finals_eligibility_X_vs_Y.json]
    31	Exit 0 = ELIGIBLE, 1 = INELIGIBLE, 2 = usage/input error.
